  "term": "thermal sensitivity",
  "definition": "Thermal sensitivity is sensitivity to temperature-based stimulation, such as heat, and can be described by the threshold at which thermal input is detected. In this source, it refers specifically to intranasal heat sensitivity as a trigeminal sensory function that varies by nasal location and is related to some measures of trigeminal and olfactory function.",
